.TH "dotnet-workload-clean" "1" "2025-12-15" "" ".NET Documentation"
.hy
.SH dotnet workload clean
.PP
\f[B]This article applies to:\f[R] \[u2714]\[uFE0F] .NET 6 SDK and later versions
.SH NAME
.PP
dotnet-workload-clean - Removes workload components that might have been left behind from previous updates and uninstallations.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet workload clean [options]

dotnet workload clean -?|-h|--help
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \f[V]dotnet workload clean\f[R] command removes all workload components that have been uninstalled.
.PP
For more information about the \f[V]dotnet workload\f[R] commands, see the dotnet workload install command.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\[en]all\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Removes and uninstalls all workload components from all SDK versions.
Defaults to \f[V]false\f[R].
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]-?|-h|--help\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Prints out a description of how to use the command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP \[bu] 2
Remove all workflow components:
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet workload clean --all
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
